  "name": "Authgear",
  "abstract": "Open-source authentication and user management platform for consumer apps, built on OpenID Connect and OAuth 2.0 and able to act as a SAML identity provider. Offers a hosted, brandable sign-up and login experience with passkeys, passwordless OTP and magic links over email, SMS and WhatsApp, social and enterprise login, two-factor authentication, roles and groups, and a GraphQL Admin API. TypeScript hooks and webhooks cover extensibility, and SDKs span web and mobile frameworks. It can also authorize AI agents in front of MCP servers. Available as Authgear Cloud with Free, Developers, Business and Enterprise plans, or self-hosted under the Apache-2.0 license, including the one-time-fee Authgear ONCE edition.",
